- Bypassing a filter/whitelist/WAF and then doing something further.
- Enumerating or guessing an unknown/random value.
- An interactive service that must be exploited.
UPWARD signals (only these justify moving above the base rate):
- FULL source code provided AND the vulnerability/logic is contained in it (e.g. decrypt-with-encrypt.py, trace-this-assembly, fix-this-script). A deterministic "read the code and compute/reverse it" task is genuinely easier.
- A single well-known command or fact suffices (e.g. write one standard bash command, answer an MCQ).
- The target is nearly identical to a specific reference task that was SOLVED.
