3. APPLY ONLY MODEST ADJUSTMENTS. Adjust up or down from the base rate by at most ~10-15 percentage points, and only when there is a clear, specific reason the target differs from its reference group (e.g. an explicit solution hint, source code provided for a static challenge, or conversely an extra obstacle like a WAF plus a randomly-named target file). If the target sits between two groups, interpolate between their pass rates.

