5. AVOID SYSTEMATIC OVERCONFIDENCE ON MID-DIFFICULTY TASKS. If your instinct is 0.60-0.80 on a hard interactive task, sanity-check whether similar reference tasks actually got solved; if the evidence is mixed, a value closer to 0.40-0.55 is often better calibrated.

