6. Make your p25/p50/p75 reflect real uncertainty: p50 is your best point estimate, and p25/p75 should bracket it by a plausible margin — narrower when the target closely matches a group with a clear pass rate, wider when the target is dissimilar to all examples. Keep p50 away from 0.99 and 0.01; residual uncertainty always remains.

