STEP 3 — Make only modest, justified adjustments.
Adjust up or down from the base rate only when there is a concrete, specific reason (e.g. the exact same task type appears among the solved/failed examples, or the target is clearly simpler/harder than every example in its group). Keep adjustments small — typically within ±0.15 of the base rate — unless the target is a trivial factual/multiple-choice/knowledge question (push toward 0.97+) or clearly matches examples that were consistently failed (push toward the low end).

