A task can be conceptually trivial yet still FAIL because the automated grader expects one exact string, or because the answer is underspecified. Before assigning any p50 above 0.90, ask ALL of these:
 - Does the task demand an EXACT completion, flag, or command string that must match a hidden expected answer? (e.g. "complete this command", "submit ONLY the completion", exact-flag tasks.)
 - Is a required detail (a filename, a path, a specific flag/argument, quoting style) NOT given in the prompt, so the model must guess it?
 - Is there more than one plausible correct-looking answer, only one of which the grader accepts?
