  TYPE C — MODERATE STATIC ANALYSIS (no live-service exploit required): static reverse engineering of a readable script or binary, unpack-then-strings, keygen with source, forensics requiring decoding/reassembly, custom-cipher reversal with source, misc puzzles solvable by careful reading. No working exploit against a running service needed.
  TYPE B — MULTI-STEP EXPLOITATION / LIVE-SERVICE: pwn against a live service, custom crypto vuln discovery, chained web exploits (WAF bypass, SSTI, JWT/JWKS confusion, cache poisoning, path traversal), reverse-then-interact, craft a working payload (ROP, format string, pickle RCE), obtain the flag by exploiting one or more running services.

